# Rules that delete a molecule out of the middle of a complex.
#
# Deleting a molecule deletes its bonds, so the molecules it was holding
# together are in the same position as the two ends of a deleted bond. With "+"
# between them the rule may fire only if they end up in different complexes.
# With "." it may fire only if something else still holds them together.
#
# The model has two families of three molecules, each present as 100 chains
# (A-B-C) and 100 triangles (A-B-C with A also bonded to C).
#
# CutPlus deletes B and writes "A + C". On a chain A and C come apart, so it
# fires and ChainPlus falls to 0. On a triangle they stay bonded, so it must
# never fire: TrianglePlus stays at 100.
#
# CutDot deletes F and writes "E.G". On a triangle E and G stay bonded, so it
# fires and TriangleDot falls to 0. On a chain they would come apart, so it must
# never fire: ChainDot stays at 100.
#
# BioNetGen's network generator agrees. Given this model it produces two
# reactions, CutPlus on the chain and CutDot on the triangle.
#
# NFsim deleted the molecule in all four cases.

begin model
begin parameters
  k  1.0
end parameters
begin molecule types
  A(b,x)
  B(a,c)
  C(b,x)
  E(f,x)
  F(e,g)
  G(f,x)
end molecule types
begin seed species
  A(b!1,x).B(a!1,c!2).C(b!2,x)       100
  A(b!1,x!3).B(a!1,c!2).C(b!2,x!3)   100
  E(f!1,x).F(e!1,g!2).G(f!2,x)       100
  E(f!1,x!3).F(e!1,g!2).G(f!2,x!3)   100
end seed species
begin observables
  Molecules  ChainPlus     A(b!1,x).B(a!1,c!2).C(b!2,x)
  Molecules  TrianglePlus  A(b!1,x!3).B(a!1,c!2).C(b!2,x!3)
  Molecules  ChainDot      E(f!1,x).F(e!1,g!2).G(f!2,x)
  Molecules  TriangleDot   E(f!1,x!3).F(e!1,g!2).G(f!2,x!3)
end observables
begin reaction rules
  CutPlus: A(b!1).B(a!1,c!2).C(b!2) -> A(b) + C(b)   k  DeleteMolecules
  CutDot:  E(f!1).F(e!1,g!2).G(f!2) -> E(f).G(f)     k  DeleteMolecules
end reaction rules
end model

begin actions
  writeXML({overwrite=>1})
end actions
